# 🐚 Day 21 – Shell Scripting Cheat Sheet

### 90 Days of DevOps | Shell Scripting Revision

> **Purpose:** Quick-reference for revising Bash and DevOps scripting concepts practiced during Days 16–20.

---

## 1. Quick Reference

| Topic       | Key Syntax                | Example                            | Purpose                        |
| ----------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Shebang     | `#!/bin/bash`             | `#!/bin/bash`                      | Defines Bash interpreter       |
| Variable    | `VAR="value"`             | `NAME="Aarti"`                     | Store data                     |
| Input       | `read`                    | `read -p "Name: " NAME`            | Accept user input              |
| Argument    | `$1`, `$2`                | `./script.sh arg1`                 | Pass values to script          |
| If          | `if [ condition ]; then`  | `if [ -f file ]; then`             | Decision making                |
| For loop    | `for i in list; do`       | `for i in 1 2 3; do`               | Repeat commands                |
| While loop  | `while [ condition ]; do` | `while [ "$COUNT" -gt 0 ]; do`     | Repeat while condition is true |
| Function    | `name() { ... }`          | `greet() { echo "Hi"; }`           | Reusable code                  |
| Grep        | `grep pattern file`       | `grep -i "error" log.txt`          | Search text                    |
| Awk         | `awk '{print $1}' file`   | `awk -F: '{print $1}' /etc/passwd` | Process columns/text           |
| Sed         | `sed 's/old/new/g' file`  | `sed -i 's/foo/bar/g' config.txt`  | Search/replace text            |
| Find        | `find path condition`     | `find /var/log -name "*.log"`      | Find files/directories         |
| Exit code   | `$?`                      | `echo $?`                          | Check previous command status  |
| Strict mode | `set -euo pipefail`       | `set -euo pipefail`                | Safer scripting                |
| Trap        | `trap 'cleanup' EXIT`     | `trap 'rm -f "$TMP"' EXIT`         | Cleanup on exit                |

