# 2. Shell Script Basics

### Shebang

```bash
#!/bin/bash
```

The shebang tells the operating system which interpreter should run the script.

### Running a Script

| Task                  | Command              |
| --------------------- | -------------------- |
| Make executable       | `chmod +x script.sh` |
| Run executable script | `./script.sh`        |
| Run using Bash        | `bash script.sh`     |

### Comments

```bash
# This is a comment

echo "Hello, DevOps!"  # Inline comment
```

