# 7. String Comparisons

| Operator | Meaning          | Example                  |
| -------- | ---------------- | ------------------------ |
| `=`      | Equal            | `[ "$NAME" = "Aarti" ]`  |
| `!=`     | Not equal        | `[ "$NAME" != "Aarti" ]` |
| `-z`     | Empty string     | `[ -z "$NAME" ]`         |
| `-n`     | Non-empty string | `[ -n "$NAME" ]`         |

### Example

```bash
if [ "$NAME" = "Aarti" ]; then
    echo "Name matches"
fi
```

