# 12. Case Statement

Useful when handling multiple choices.

```bash
case "$CHOICE" in
    y)
        echo "Yes"
        ;;
    n)
        echo "No"
        ;;
    *)
        echo "Invalid choice"
        ;;
esac
```

| Symbol      | Purpose    |
| ----------- | ---------- |
| `case`      | Start      |
| `y)` / `n)` | Pattern    |
| `;;`        | End option |
| `*`         | Default    |
| `esac`      | End        |

