# 34. Error Handling

### `set -e`

Exit script when a command fails.

```bash
set -e
```

### `set -u`

Treat unset variables as errors.

```bash
set -u
```

### `pipefail`

Detect failures inside pipelines.

```bash
set -o pipefail
```

### Strict Mode

```bash
#!/bin/bash

set -euo pipefail
```

| Option     | Meaning                  |
| ---------- | ------------------------ |
| `-e`       | Exit when command fails  |
| `-u`       | Error on unset variables |
| `pipefail` | Detect pipeline failures |

