# 36. `trap`

Use `trap` for cleanup when a script exits.

```bash
TMP="/tmp/devops-temp"

touch "$TMP"

cleanup() {
    rm -f "$TMP"
}

trap 'cleanup' EXIT
```

| Command   | Purpose           |
| --------- | ----------------- |
| `trap`    | Catch an event    |
| `EXIT`    | When script exits |
| `cleanup` | Cleanup function  |

---

# 37. Practical Script Template

```bash
#!/bin/bash

set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    echo "Usage: $0 <argument>"
    exit 1
}

cleanup() {
    echo "Cleaning up..."
}

trap 'cleanup' EXIT

if [ $# -lt 1 ]; then
    usage
fi

INPUT="$1"

echo "Processing: $INPUT"
```

